  body: "# Appointee acting for a claimant in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nAn appointment in the described
    procedure allows a person or body to act for someone unable to act for themselves; an appointee assumes the
    claimant’s responsibilities, including disclosing changes.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nAn informal helper
    is not automatically an appointee. Existing legal appointments, age and appointment conditions, territorial
    differences and revocation provisions require separate review. This is distinct from directing payment to another
    person.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 08250, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=34)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08251, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=34)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08252, PDF page 34](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=34)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08254, PDF page 35](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=35)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch8` PDF SHA-256: `8bf08435715020c8cc57be24e06e6fd8c90d99232254004ba67d1c5dfc3dd864`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `e6c5a71afbf2536bc63a91a4389284b2b6b8aaaa8bff015d4f34b478f77b28cc`.\n"
